w: 1.~Jer- u- sa- lem the gol- den, with milk and hon- ey blest, 
w: 2.~They stand, those halls of Zi- on, all ju- bi- lant with song, 
w: 3.~There is the throne of Da- vid, and there, from care re- leased, 
w: 4.~O sweet and bless- èd coun- try, the home of God's e- lect! 
w: 5.~Brief life is here our por- tion, brief sor- row, short lived care; 
w: 6.~That we should look, poor wan- d’rers, to have our home on high!
w: 7.~And how we watch and stru- ggle, and now we live in hope,
w: 8.~For thee, O dear, dear coun- try, mine eyes their vig- ils keep;
w: 9.~O one, O on- ly man- sion! O par- a- dise of joy!
w: 10.~Je- ru- sa- lem the glor- ious! Glo- ry of the e- lect!
w: 11.~Je- ru- sa- lem, the on- ly, that look'st from heaven be- low,
w: 12.~Je- ru- sa- lem, e- xul- ting on that se- cu- rest shore,
w: 13.~But yet with faith I ven- ture and hope up- on the way,
w: 14.~When in His strength I stru- ggle, for ver- y joy I leap;
w: 15.~O sweet and bless- èd coun- try, shall I e'er see thy face?
