w: Be- neath thy con- tem- pla- tion sink heart and voice op- pressed. 
w: And bright with man- y'an an- gel, and all the mar- tyr throng; 
w: The shout of them that tri- umph, the song of them that feast; 
w: O sweet and bless- èd coun- try, that ea- ger hearts ex- pect! 
w: The life that knows no end- ing, the tear- less life, is there. 
w: That worms should seek for dwel- lings be- yond the star- ry sky!
w: And Zi- on in her an- guish with Ba- by- lon must cope;
w: For ver- y love, be- hold- ing, thy hap- py name, they weep:
w: Where tears are ev- er ban- ished, and smiles have no al- loy;
w: O dear and fu- ture vi- sion that ea- ger hearts ex- pect!
w: In thee is all my glo- ry, in me is all my woe!
w: I hope thee, wish thee, sing thee, and love thee ev- er- more!
w: For those pe- ren- nial guer- dons I la- bor night and day.
w: When in my sin I tot- ter, I weep, or try to weep:
w: O sweet and bless- èd coun- try, shall I e'er win thy grace?
