w: What ra- dian- cy of glo- ry, what bliss be- yond com- pare. 
w: The pas- tures of the bless- èd are decked in glor- ious sheen. 
w: And won for them for- ev- er their gleam- ing robes of white. 
w: Who art, with God the Fa- ther, and Spir- it, ev- er blessed. 
w: For mor- tals and for sin- ners, a man- sion with the blest. 
w: Of full and ev- er- last- ing, and pas- sion- less re- nown.
w: And they that know and see Him shall have Him for their own.
w: And me- di- cine in sick- ness, and love, and life, and rest.
w: His laud and be- ne- dic- tion thy ran- somed peo- ple raise.
w: To thee my thoughts are kind- led, and strive, and pant, and yearn.
w: Till flesh and earth re- turn me to earth and flesh a- gain.
w: My mer- it is de- struc- tion, a child of wrath am I.
w: Bore with me in de- fi- lement, and from de- fi- lement laved.
w: And Da- vid's ro- yal foun- tain purge ev- ery stain a- way.
w: O shall I e'er win the prize? O tell me, tell me, Yes!
